ow to generate an SDK yourself using the provided Swagger specification."},"692":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-7","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#official-sdks","content":"We maintain several pre-built SDKs for various programming languages. All of these SDKs are generated from our Swagger files and are optimized for seamless integration into your projects."},"693":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-8","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#official-sdks","content":"**Golang SDK**: tonapi-go"},"694":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-9","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#official-sdks","content":"**JS/TS Client (dApp free limits, @ton/core compatible)**: @ton-api/client"},"695":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-10","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#ton-adapter-compatible-with-tonton","content":"The @ton-api/ton-adapter allows you to integrate TonAPI projects that use `@ton/ton`, enhancing your application with additional blockchain features while maintaining compatibility with `@ton/ton`."},"696":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-11","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#third-party-sdks","content":"These SDKs are maintained by the community and provide additional language support:"},"697":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-12","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#third-party-sdks","content":"**Python SDK**: pytonapi on GitHub"},"698":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-13","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#third-party-sdks","content":"**Java SDK**: tonapi4j on GitHub"},"699":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-14","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generating-an-sdk-using-the-openapi-generator","content":"If you prefer to generate an SDK yourself, you can do so using the TonAPI OpenAPI specification. Follow these steps:"},"700":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-15","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#install-the-openapi-generator-cli-tool","content":"Install the OpenAPI generator globally using `npm`:"},"701":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-16","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"Use the command below to generate the SDK. The example is for Ruby, but you can specify a different language by changing the `-g` (generator) parameter."},"702":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-17","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"**Note:** Replace `/path/to/output` with the actual directory path where you want to generate the SDK."},"703":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-18","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"If you encounter issues during client generation for certain languages (for example, due to multiple tags per operation or possible future enum value additions), consider using the following options:"},"704":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-19","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"`--openapi-normalizer KEEP_ONLY_FIRST_TAG_IN_OPERATION=true`  \nThis flag helps if the Swagger file contains multiple tags for a single operation and your SDK generator/language has trouble with that (it keeps only the first tag)."},"705":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-20","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"`--additional-properties=enumUnknownDefaultCase=true`  \nThis flag ensures your generated SDKs will gracefully handle new/unknown enum values in the future by mapping them to a default enum case such as `UNKNOWN_DEFAULT` (supported in Java, Kotlin, TypeScript, Swift, etc)."},"706":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-21","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"You can combine these options in a single command, for example:"},"707":{"id":"/tonapi/sdk-22","page_id":"/tonapi/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/sdk#generate-the-sdk","content":"To ru