 crucial for any production usage."},"725":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-15","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#authorization","content":"TonAPI looks for an API key in two places in the following order:"},"726":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-16","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#authorization","content":"In the Authorization header with the \"Bearer scheme\".\nFor example:"},"727":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-17","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#authorization","content":"In the \"token\" parameter of the query string.\nFor example:"},"728":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-18","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#server-sent-events","content":"SSE methods response with `text/event-stream` Content-Type and communications happen in a text format.\nEach API method sends two types of events: **heartbeat** and **message**.\nThe \"heartbeat\" event occurs every 5 seconds when nothing else happens\nand is a signal that everything is OK with an underlying TCP connection.\nThe \"message\" event carries important information and its \"data\" always contains a JSON representation of a message."},"729":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-19","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#server-sent-events","content":"A golang example of working with SSE method."},"730":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-20","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-new-blocks","content":"API method GET `https://tonapi.io/v2/sse/blocks?workchain=<...>` sends notifications about new blocks in the given workchain.\nThe `workchain` parameter is optional and TonAPI will stream blocks from all workchains if it's not provided."},"731":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-21","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-new-blocks","content":"A response example:"},"732":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-22","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-finalized-transactions","content":"This GET method takes in a list of account IDs  and an optional list of operations."},"733":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-23","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-finalized-transactions","content":"| Query parameter | Description                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| accounts        | A comma-separated list of account IDs. A special value of \"accounts\" is **ALL**. TonAPI will stream transactions for all accounts in this case. |","table":"table-0"},"734":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-24","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-finalized-transactions","content":"| Query parameter | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| operations      | A comma-separated list of operations, which makes it possible to get transactions based on the first 4 bytes of a message body of an inbound message. Each operation is a string containing either one of the supported names or a hex string representing a message operation opcode which is an unsigned 32-bit integer. A hex string must start with \"0x\" prefix and have exactly 8 hex digits.  An example of \"operations\" is `&operations=JettonTransfer,0x0524c7ae,StonfiSwap`. The advantage of using hex strings is that it's possible to get transactions for operations that are not yet present on the list. |","table":"table-0"},"735":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-25","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-finalized-transactions","content":"Then it starts streaming finalized transactions that belong to the given list of accounts."},"736":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-26","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-finalized-transactions","content":"A response example:"},"737":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-27","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-traces","content":"A trace in the TON blockchain is a series of transactions caused by one inbound message.\nIt usually consists of multiple transactions on different accounts.\nOnce a trace completes, TonAPI sends the trace's hash and a list of involved accounts to all subscribers who are interested in any of these accounts."},"738":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-28","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-traces","content":"This GET method takes in a comma-separated list of account IDs as \"accounts\" query parameter."},"739":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-29","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-traces","content":"A special value of \"accounts\" is **ALL**. TonAPI will stream all traces in this case."},"740":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-30","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-traces","content":"A response example:"},"741":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-31","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-pending-messages-mempool","content":"API method GET 'https://tonapi.io/v2/sse/mempool' immediately starts streaming BOCs of pending inbound messages:"},"742":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-32","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#real-time-notifications-about-pending-messages-mempool","content":"\"boc\" parameter is a serialized instance of a tlb.Message."},"743":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-33","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#subscribe-to-a-list-of-accounts","content":"Because a flow of pending messages could be quite high, TonAPI has a way to provide a list of accounts that you are interested in by using \"accounts\" query parameter:"},"744":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-34","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#subscribe-to-a-list-of-accounts","content":"GET 'https://tonapi.io/v2/sse/mempool?accounts=comma-separated-list-of-accounts'."},"745":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-35","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#subscribe-to-a-list-of-accounts","content":"In this case,\nTonAPI emulates a message to get a list of involved accounts.\nIf any of them is on the list you provided, TonAPI will send a message to you along with a full list of accounts involved in this trace."},"746":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-36","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"TonAPI supports a JSON-RPC protocol over a websocket connection. It is available at `wss://tonapi.io/v2/websocket`.\nSupported methods are:"},"747":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-37","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"**subscribe_block**"},"748":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-38","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"**subscribe_account**"},"749":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-39","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"**subscribe_trace**"},"750":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-40","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"**subscribe_mempool**"},"751":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-41","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#websocket","content":"A golang example of working with websocket."},"752":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-42","page_id":"/tonapi/streaming-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tonapi/streaming-api#subscribe_block-method","content":"`subscribe_block` starts streaming new blocks.\nIt is possible to specify a workchain by using \"params\" argument to limit the stream to a specific workchain."},"753":{"id":"/tonapi/streaming-api-43","page_